{"patch":{"config":{"title":"Antranig Basman","baseURL":"https://ponder.org.uk","defaultContentLanguage":"en","mainSections":["post","posts"],"author":{"name":"Antranig Basman","website":"/","email":"amb26web@ponder.org.uk","twitter":"amb26ponder"},"params":{"homeTitle":"Antranig Basman","subtitle":"Building habitable technologies","bio":"img/20230209_135356 - bio - cropped.jpg","logo":"img/pond.jpg","favicon":"img/favicon.ico","dateFormat":"January 2, 2006","comments":true,"socialShare":true,"showRelatedPosts":true,"commentsLayer":"beautifulWend.comments.giscus","customCSS":["css/ponder.css"],"mediaIcons":[{"title":"Twitter profile","href":"http://twitter.com/amb26ponder","icon":"fab fa-twitter"},{"title":"Send me a message","href":"mailto:amb26webpage@ponder.org.uk","icon":"fa fa-envelope"},{"title":"Antranig's GitHub profile","href":"http://github.com/amb26","icon":"fab fa-github-alt"},{"title":"My papers on DBLP","href":"https://dblp.org/pid/68/5013.html","icon":"fa fa-university"},{"title":"My LinkedIn profile","href":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/antranigbasman/","icon":"fab fa-linkedin"}],"giscus":{"repo":"amb26/ponder","repoId":"R_kgDOOKllGA","category":"Announcements","categoryId":"DIC_kwDOOKllGM4CvhAS"}},"menu":{"main":[{"name":"Posts","url":"post","weight":1},{"name":"WiP","url":"wip","weight":1},{"name":"Docs","identifier":"docs","url":"docs","weight":3},{"name":"Fluid Signals","parent":"docs","url":"docs/fluid-signals","weight":1},{"name":"Fluid Integration Language","parent":"docs","url":"docs/fluid-integration-language","weight":2},{"name":"Fluid View","parent":"docs","url":"docs/fluid-view","weight":3},{"name":"Fluid PTF","parent":"docs","url":"docs/fluid-ptf","weight":4},{"name":"Fluid tldraw integration","parent":"docs","url":"docs/fluid-tldraw","weight":5},{"name":"wend","parent":"docs","url":"docs/wend","weight":6},{"name":"About","url":"page/about/","weight":3},{"name":"Communities","url":"communities","weight":4},{"name":"Projects","url":"projects","weight":5},{"name":"Terms","url":"term","weight":5}]}},"features":{"selfHosted":true,"hljs":true}},"pages":[{"kind":"page","type":"page","section":"","title":"Edit in Infusion - Privacy Policy","relPermalink":"/edit-in-infusion-privacy/","permalink":"https://ponder.org.uk/edit-in-infusion-privacy/","outputPath":"/edit-in-infusion-privacy/index.html","params":{"title":"Edit in Infusion - Privacy Policy","subtitle":"The Chrome extension \"Edit in Infusion\"","comments":false,"socialShare":false},"sourcePath":"content/edit-in-infusion-privacy.md","content":"<p><em>Last updated 20 November 2026</em></p>\n<p>“Edit in Infusion” is a Chrome extension for editing a statically published website in place, on pages which\nadvertise the sources they were built from. This policy describes what it handles, where that is kept, and where it\nis sent. In short: it has no server of its own, collects nothing about you, and sends what you edit only to the\nGitHub repository of the site you are editing, when you ask it to.</p>\n<h3 id=\"when-it-does-anything\"><a class=\"infusion-docs-anchor\" aria-label=\"When it does anything\" href=\"#when-it-does-anything\"><span class=\"octicon octicon-link\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span></a>When it does anything</h3>\n<p>The extension does nothing on a website until you click its button there. Clicking asks your permission to access\nthat site. If you grant it, the extension runs on that site’s pages from then on, so that they can show edits you\nhave made which are not yet published. You can withdraw that access at any time from the extension’s options page,\nor from Chrome’s own extension settings. On every other site, it does nothing.</p>\n<h3 id=\"what-it-handles\"><a class=\"infusion-docs-anchor\" aria-label=\"What it handles\" href=\"#what-it-handles\"><span class=\"octicon octicon-link\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span></a>What it handles</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>The pages of sites you enable it on.</strong> It reads the page’s <em>linkage record</em>, a small description the site\npublishes of the files the page was built from, and the content of the page, in order to show your edits in it. It\ndoes not read or record anything else about your browsing.</li>\n<li><strong>Your edits.</strong> The text of the files you edit, held until they are published.</li>\n<li><strong>A GitHub access token</strong> which you provide, so that it can read and commit the site’s files on your behalf.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"where-it-is-kept\"><a class=\"infusion-docs-anchor\" aria-label=\"Where it is kept\" href=\"#where-it-is-kept\"><span class=\"octicon octicon-link\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span></a>Where it is kept</h3>\n<p>Everything is kept in your own browser, in the extension’s private storage:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Your GitHub token is kept in the extension’s local storage. It is never made visible to the pages you edit.</li>\n<li>Your edits are kept in the extension’s IndexedDB storage until the site is seen to have published them, or you\ndiscard them.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The extension has no server of its own and no analytics. Nothing is synchronised between your devices.</p>\n<h3 id=\"where-it-is-sent\"><a class=\"infusion-docs-anchor\" aria-label=\"Where it is sent\" href=\"#where-it-is-sent\"><span class=\"octicon octicon-link\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span></a>Where it is sent</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>To GitHub</strong> (<a href=\"http://api.github.com\">api.github.com</a>), using your token: requests to read the files of the repository a page names, and,\nonly when you press <em>Commit</em>, a commit of your edit to that repository. Such requests are governed by\n<a href=\"https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement\">GitHub’s privacy statement</a>.\nA commit is public if the repository is, and records your GitHub identity as its author.</li>\n<li><strong>To the site you are editing</strong>: requests for files the site itself publishes - the description of its latest\nbuild, the code it renders its pages with, and the data of the page being edited - in the same way that viewing\nthe site does.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Nothing is sent anywhere else, and nothing is sold or shared with anyone.</p>\n<h3 id=\"removing-your-data\"><a class=\"infusion-docs-anchor\" aria-label=\"Removing your data\" href=\"#removing-your-data\"><span class=\"octicon octicon-link\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span></a>Removing your data</h3>\n<p>Choosing <em>Forget token</em> in the extension’s options removes your token. Discarding an edit removes it. Uninstalling\nthe extension removes everything it has stored.</p>\n<h3 id=\"contact\"><a class=\"infusion-docs-anchor\" aria-label=\"Contact\" href=\"#contact\"><span class=\"octicon octicon-link\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span></a>Contact</h3>\n<p>Questions about this policy may be sent to <a href=\"mailto:amb26web@ponder.org.uk\">amb26web@ponder.org.uk</a>. The extension’s\nsource is part of <a href=\"https://github.com/fluid-project/infusion-6\">Infusion 6</a>, in its <code>extension/</code> directory.</p>\n","summary":"Last updated 20 November 2026 “Edit in Infusion” is a Chrome extension for editing a statically published website in place, on pages which advertise the sources they were built from. This policy describes what it handles, where that is kept, and where it is sent. In short: it has no server of its own, collects nothing about you, and sends what you edit only to the GitHub repository of the site you are editing, when you ask it to.","summaryText":"Last updated 20 November 2026 “Edit in Infusion” is a Chrome extension for editing a statically published website in place, on pages which advertise the sources they were built from. This policy describes what it handles, where that is kept, and where it is sent. In short: it has no server of its own, collects nothing about you, and sends what you edit only to the GitHub repository of the site you are editing, when you ask it to.","truncated":true,"prevInSection":{"title":"Infusion","relPermalink":"/infusion/"},"nextInSection":{"title":"My Communities","relPermalink":"/communities/"}}],"shared":{"menu":[{"name":"Posts","url":"post","weight":1,"children":[]},{"name":"WiP","url":"wip","weight":1,"children":[]},{"name":"About","url":"page/about/","weight":3,"children":[]},{"name":"Docs","identifier":"docs","url":"docs","weight":3,"children":[{"name":"Fluid Signals","parent":"docs","url":"docs/fluid-signals","weight":1,"children":[]},{"name":"Fluid Integration Language","parent":"docs","url":"docs/fluid-integration-language","weight":2,"children":[]},{"name":"Fluid View","parent":"docs","url":"docs/fluid-view","weight":3,"children":[]},{"name":"Fluid PTF","parent":"docs","url":"docs/fluid-ptf","weight":4,"children":[]},{"name":"Fluid tldraw integration","parent":"docs","url":"docs/fluid-tldraw","weight":5,"children":[]},{"name":"wend","parent":"docs","url":"docs/wend","weight":6,"children":[]}]},{"name":"Communities","url":"communities","weight":4,"children":[]},{"name":"Projects","url":"projects","weight":5,"children":[]},{"name":"Terms","url":"term","weight":5,"children":[]}],"lang":"en","buildYear":2026,"relatedIndex":[{"relPermalink":"/","title":"Antranig Basman","kind":"home","params":{}},{"relPermalink":"/post/","title":"post","kind":"section","params":{}},{"relPermalink":"/wip/","title":"wip","kind":"section","params":{}},{"relPermalink":"/wip/page/2/","title":"wip","kind":"section","params":{}},{"relPermalink":"/docs/","title":"docs","kind":"section","params":{}},{"relPermalink":"/page/","title":"page","kind":"section","params":{}},{"relPermalink":"/term/","title":"term","kind":"section","params":{}},{"relPermalink":"/term/page/2/","title":"term","kind":"section","params":{}},{"relPermalink":"/post/2026-06-28-fully-deferred-stabilization/","title":"Bridging the gap between static and dynamic analysis through fully deferred stabilization","kind":"page","params":{}},{"relPermalink":"/wip/2026-05-25-towards-deferred-stabilisati